--
N5008 [expr.prim.lambda.closure]/4, [expr.prim.lambda.capture]: a generic
lambda's call operator is a member function template.  A generic lambda with
a by-reference capture or in a member function was kept on the
function-pointer lowering, with every `auto' fixed to `signed int'; this
program crashed the front end (bin53).  Such lambdas are now lowered to a
closure with a template operator() (typecheck_expr_lambda,
generic_closure_eligible), like other generic lambdas.  Lambdas that use
`this' explicitly or call member functions stay on the function-pointer
lowering.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program (-std=c++14), and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
